# Keep the Docker build context small.
#
# The working tree is ~1 GB, almost all of it already-compiled objects and the
# 68 MB test corpus. The build needs src/, include/, external/ and
# CMakeLists.txt - about 8 MB. Without this file every build would upload the
# lot, over and over.
#
# Everything is excluded first, then the few things the build genuinely reads
# are allowed back in. A denylist would silently grow stale the moment somebody
# adds a new build directory.

*

!CMakeLists.txt
!src/
!include/
!external/
!docker/
# ndixput.py only - it is what patches the guest's /etc/rc so NDIX configures
# its own network at boot. The rest of tools/ is not needed in the image.
!tools/ndix/ndixput.py

# ...but not these, even inside the directories allowed above.
external/**/build/
external/**/.git
docker/disk/*.session
docker/*.md
